% Software-intensive systems ranging from standard software applications to AI agents and autonomous cyber-physical systems are delivering functionality and services with increasingly complex normative implications of a legal, social, ethical, empathetic, and cultural (SLEEC) nature~\cite{Inverardi22,Boltz24GYILLZ}. Distilling these implications into a valid and comprehensive set of \emph{SLEEC requirements} for a system under development has been the subject of significant activity in recent years. 

