\subsection{\label{seven} Pathways with seven reactions}

Two non-oxidative glycolytic pathways with seven reactions were found in the expanded reaction network and are shown in Figure \ref{fig: 7reaction_7biphosphate} and Figure \ref{fig: 7reaction_5biphosphate}. The first uses sedoheptulose-1,7-biphosphate, while the second uses xylulose-1,5-biphosphate. The first pathway has been studied in \cite{nog_model_implemen2} under laboratory conditions and was reported to "overcome bottlenecks from the previously reported non-oxidative glycolysis cycles." Both pathways use only four of the seven templated enzymatic reactions used to expand the reaction network: aldolase, aldose-ketose isomerase, phosphohydrolase, and phosphoketolase.

\begin{figure}
