\begin{equation*}
    \Delta_r G = -RT \ln \left(\frac{[\text{S7P}][\text{P}_i]}{[\text{SBP}][H_2O]}\right)
\end{equation*}
A concentration ratio of only $1.26$ for [SBP]/[S7P] moves the reaction to thermal equilibrium at $300$ K, considering the unit activities of the water and phosphate molecules. The corresponding value for the ratio of [XBP]/[X5P] so that the reaction is in equilibrium is $19.32$. These concentration gradients can be maintained by the active transport of the molecules involved in the reactions.

