\subsubsection{Pathways to 3-hydroxypropioic acid}
Since 3-hydroxypropionic acid is a molecule containing three carbon atoms, the optimal efficiency would be achieved when two molecules are produced from one molecule of fructose-6-phosphate, leading to the overall reaction:
\begin{equation}
    \text{F6P } + \text{H}_2\text{O} \longrightarrow 2\text{HPA } + \text{P}_i \text{\hspace{2cm}} \Delta_r G = -114.428 \text{ kJ mol}^{-1}
    \label{hpa}
\end{equation}
