    \begin{abstract}
        For any homogeneous space of a real semisimple algebraic group $G$, we define an exponent with multiple interpretations from representation theory and group theory. As an application, we give a temperedness criterion for $\Lspace^2(G/H)$ for any closed subgroup $H$ of $G$, which extends the existing ones of Benoist-Kobayashi for connected subgroups and Lutsko-Weich-Wolf for discrete subgroups.
