\section{Conclusion}
Quantum circuit optimization is critical for selecting the best circuit implementation for a given algorithm.  This paper explores the role of phase-polynomial optimization in full-circuit optimization and improves upon the state-of-the-art without requiring an exhaustive search. Additionally, we provide an approach to deliver hardware-friendly recurring phase polynomial blocks. 


