In this section, we illustrate and validate our theoretical results through two numerical simulations. In particular, we show the behavior of LDP-SGD and LDP-ASGD estimators in both strongly and non-strongly convex cases. To evaluate the results, we define the parameter distance of an estimator \( \hat{\theta} \) to the optimum \( \theta^* \) as \( \mathbb{E}(\|\hat{\theta} - \theta^*\|^2) \). Similarly, we define the loss distance to the optimum as \( \mathbb{E}(\|F(\hat{\theta}) - F(\theta^*)\|^2) \).


