In this section, we demonstrate the proposed LDP-SGD and LDP-ASGD algorithms using the synthetic data based on the US insurance dataset, which includes health insurance premium charge records in the United States. The  dataset captures various factors influencing medical costs, including age, gender, body mass index (BMI), number of children, smoking status, region, medical history, exercise frequency, occupation, and type of insurance plan. It was generated by randomly sampling 1,000,000 records to provide a comprehensive representation of the insured population. The dataset is publicly available at \textsf{https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sridharstreaks/insurance-data-for-machine-learning}.

