     \caption{If edge $(\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2)$ traverses any passage, $\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2$ are in different Gabriel cells. The reverse also holds on the condition that $(\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2)$ is feasible. If $\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2$ are in different cells but $(\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2)$ passes no passages, $(\mathbf{x}_1, \mathbf{x}_2)$ must collide with obstacles.}
