\subsubsection{Tokenizer performance}
T2M-GPT \cite{zhang2023generating} used the vector quantization (VQ) \cite{van2017neural} to serve as the tokenizer while MoMask \cite{guo2024momask} proposed to use residual vector quantization (R-VQ) as a tokenizer. We train both of them on our dataset so that T2M-GPT \cite{zhang2023generating} and MoMask \cite{guo2024momask} can use them as model components. Therefore, we also show the reconstruction performances of VQ and R-VQ (Table \ref{tab:tokenizer}), which are measured by the reconstruction Fréchet Inception Distance (rFID) and the Mean Per Joint Position Error (MPJPE).


