Generative design refers to algorithms like generative adversarial networks (GANs) and evolutionary algorithms, which can create a wide variety of design alternatives based on user-defined parameters and constraints\cite{yuan2022deep}. These algorithms explore the solution space by considering factors such as spatial constraints, functional requirements, aesthetic preferences, and material properties. By generating multiple iterations of a design, generative design allows designers to consider various options quickly, making it easier to identify the most suitable layout and design choices for a specific project. For example, in residential design, generative design can create a range of floor plans based on the size of the family, the number of rooms, or specific preferences for room configuration (Figure \ref{fig:case_1}).

