Here, two points are worthy of mention. First, the cooperation levels observed for a fully occupied lattice are consistent with previous findings using the same Q-learning framework~\cite{wang2022levy, yang2024interaction}. 
Second, we observe that across all densities, cooperation does not fall to zero as the temptation to defect, $b$, increases. This stands in stark contrast to the spatial PD played with fixed update rules, such as those based on the Fermi-Dirac transition probabilities, where cooperators rapidly go extinct under similar conditions~\cite{perc2008social}.
