	\arrow["{\tau_{\tilde\splitt_c}^{\eta_A^B}\;*\;\pair_A^B}", Rightarrow, from=1-1, to=1-5]
	\arrow["{(\pair_A^B)^\lilbullet c\;*\;\beta_A^B}", Rightarrow, from=1-5, to=1-9]
\end{tikzcd}\] and observe that: $$P_{C}*(\splitt_c\pair_A^B\Longrightarrow(\pair_A^B)^\lilbullet c)= (\eta_A^B*\pair_A^B)(\pair_A^B*\beta_A^B)=1_{\pair_A^B}$$ since, being the given $(\pair_A^B,\pi_A^B,\eta_A^B,\beta_A^B)$ an equivalence, we can assume without loss of generality that it is in fact an adjoint equivalence---up to replacing $\eta_A^B$ with a parallel 2-cell \cite{MR2664622}, \cite{MR0220789}, \cite[Chapter 6]{MR0371990}. Therefore, referring to the diagram: % https://q.uiver.app/#
\begin{equation}\label{reindexingsigma}\begin{tikzcd}[column sep=scriptsize,row sep=small]
