\noindent\textbf{Re-indexing structure and arrow object structure on display maps.} Without delving too deeply into the details\footnotemark[4], we state that the 1-cells of $\mathcal{D}$ can be endowed with a 1- and 2-dimensional re-indexing structure, as well as with a structure of arrow objects, such that the compatibilities outlined in the third and fourth points of Definition \ref{split display map 2-category} are satisfied. We only mention that the re-indexing of a display map $P_A:\Gamma.A\to\Gamma$ along a 1-cell $f:\Delta\to\Gamma$ of $\grpd$ is obtained by applying the Grothendieck construction to the pseudofunctor $\begin{tikzcd}[cramped,column sep=small,row sep=tiny]
	\Delta && \Gamma && \grpd,
