%\fnote{}{Email: }


\vskip 5mm

\begin{abstract}\noindent
We compute an explicit rank bound on the Picard group of the compact surfaces, which can serve as the base of an elliptic Calabi-Yau variety with canonical singularities. To bound the Picard rank from above, we develop a novel strategy in birational geometry, motivated in part by the physics of six-dimensional vacua of F-theory as discussed in a companion paper~\cite{steft} to this one. The derivation of the concrete bound illustrates the strategy and clarifies the origin of the boundedness. 


\end{abstract}


