=
\cC_{--}.
$$
Observe that $X\in\cC_{+-}$ being a generator means that the map
$\End_\cC(1_{+})\otimes \End_\cC(1_-)\to Z(\End_\cC(X))$ given by 
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:ZEndXIso}
\tikzmath{
\draw[rounded corners=5pt, dotted] (-.5,-.5) rectangle (.5,.5);
\roundNbox{}{(0,0)}{.3}{0}{0}{$x$}
}\,
\otimes 
\,\tikzmath{
\fill[rounded corners=5pt, gray!50] (-.5,-.5) rectangle (.5,.5);
\roundNbox{fill=white}{(0,0)}{.3}{0}{0}{$y$}
}\,
\longmapsto
\,\tikzmath{
\begin{scope}
\clip[rounded corners=5pt] (-1,-.5) rectangle (1,.5);
\fill[gray!50] (0,-.5) rectangle (1,.5);    
\end{scope}
